X Server for Android, using SDL 1.2 backend.

You need to compile this code using SDL downloaded from

https://github.com/pelya/commandergenius

Compilation instructions:

https://github.com/pelya/commandergenius/tree/sdl_android/project/jni/application/xserver

To compile and run a test build of XSDL for Linux, run commands:

```
sudo apt-get install libsdl1.2-dev
sudo apt-get build-dep xserver-xorg-core
./build-xsdl-for-linux.sh
./start-linux.sh
```

Then you can run this command to test it:
```
export DISPLAY=:1111
xfwm4 &
xterm
```

SDL creates a screen buffer in memory, returned by SDL_SetVideoMode().

XSDL code copies video data from X screen buffer to SDL screen buffer on each frame,
then SDL copies it into OpenGL texture on each call of SDL_Flip().

Shared memory is used for X apps to write directly to X screen buffer,
instead of transferring video data over TCP socket.
It is implemented by android-shmem library.

And XSDL does not support any OpenGL acceleration for X apps, even though it uses OpenGL ES internally.
